# Workers static assets headers (https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers/).
# Applies only to files served from build/client, never to Worker (SSR/API) responses,
# so HTML keeps its no-cache policy. Everything under /assets/ is content-hashed by Vite:
# a new build gets new URLs, so a year-long immutable cache is safe and removes the
# per-navigation revalidation of every chunk. sw.js, the manifest and icons keep the default.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Security headers for every static asset.
#
# These files are served before the Worker runs, so the headers
# `workers/lib/security-headers.ts` applies never reach them. This block repeats
# BASE_SECURITY_HEADERS so every response carries the same set;
# `test/security-headers.test.ts` fails if the two drift.
#
# The zone-level HSTS setting (security_header, currently include_subdomains:
# false) overrides Strict-Transport-Security on every response, Worker or
# asset. Changing it is a zone-wide decision for the account owner, not code.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
